WEBVTT

00:02.690 --> 00:07.080
Want to take out the unique monster, 
Wethermon the Tombguard,

00:07.080 --> 00:08.490
with just the three of us?

00:08.480 --> 00:14.530
Pencil Knight

00:14.770 --> 00:18.040
Huh?! A unique monster?!

00:18.040 --> 00:19.240
Right.

00:19.240 --> 00:22.500
Wethermon is likely a 
"special condition" type.

00:22.780 --> 00:25.160
Possibilities that come to mind...

00:25.160 --> 00:28.040
"Pick up or destroy a 
particular in-game object."

00:28.040 --> 00:29.480
"Last a certain length of time."

00:29.480 --> 00:31.510
"Survive a particular attack."

00:31.510 --> 00:38.140
Pencil Knight

00:31.510 --> 00:38.140
Sunraku

00:31.510 --> 00:38.140
Katzo Tataki

00:32.180 --> 00:36.200
You occasionally see "reason with 
him in the middle of battle," too.

00:36.200 --> 00:38.130
Any idea on what the condition is?

00:38.630 --> 00:40.810
I've tried a few different things,

00:41.170 --> 00:43.500
and I think it's "Last a 
certain length of time."

00:44.190 --> 00:49.560
<i>Wethermon the Tombguard's combat 
conditions change as time passes.</i>

00:50.120 --> 00:54.210
<i>First, we need to survive 
the ten minutes of Phase 1.</i>

00:59.930 --> 01:04.250
<i>I won't let your memories be sad ones.</i>

01:08.400 --> 01:10.220
Please put Wethermon...

01:10.610 --> 01:13.480
Please put my love to rest.

02:51.500 --> 02:57.000
<b>Putting Feelings Into a Moment, Part 2</b>

03:02.370 --> 03:03.410
What's this?

03:03.640 --> 03:05.410
A Rebirth Tearjewel?

03:05.410 --> 03:08.420
<b>Rebirth Tearjewel</b>

03:05.900 --> 03:07.680
It's a resurrection item.

03:08.680 --> 03:13.220
If you use it on a disabled 
player within ten seconds,

03:13.220 --> 03:17.130
you can revive them with full HP.

03:17.370 --> 03:19.090
Oh, you can do that?

03:19.090 --> 03:20.680
That's a god-tier item, then!

03:22.870 --> 03:25.010
I went from town to town this morning

03:25.010 --> 03:27.560
and bought all twelve that were for sale.

03:29.050 --> 03:30.860
Use them carefully, now.

03:31.600 --> 03:34.360
They cost four million mahni apiece.

03:34.360 --> 03:37.110
Four million?!

03:37.520 --> 03:40.440
We'll get four Rebirth Tearjewels each.

03:40.440 --> 03:43.960
Then there's this, which lets 
you revive at half your max HP—

03:43.120 --> 03:49.880
<b>Divine Lifesalve
</b>A secret formula sealed within specially treated glass.
When used on a disabled target within ten seconds,
it revives them with half of their max HP. 
Life is an ever-repeating cycle,
but what a noble thing it is to fight against the tide!
<b>Accept</b>

03:43.960 --> 03:46.550
the Divine Lifesalve—
of which we each get five.

03:45.090 --> 03:47.860
<b>Divine Lifesalve</b>

03:47.870 --> 03:50.410
That's the max number of extra 
lives you can get in this game.

03:51.160 --> 03:55.130
We'll use these 27 resurrection items 
to challenge Wethermon the Tombguard.

03:56.080 --> 03:56.870
Right.

03:57.730 --> 04:01.240
Sunraku-kun will take point on 
holding off Wethermon's attacks.

04:01.240 --> 04:05.890
If you get killed, Katzo-kun or I will 
revive you and take over for a bit.

04:06.140 --> 04:10.270
And the same goes if one 
of us bites it, right?

04:10.490 --> 04:11.630
Yes.

04:11.630 --> 04:16.650
To achieve our goal of surviving long 
enough against the Colossus, Wethermon,

04:16.650 --> 04:17.780
this is the only way.

04:21.700 --> 04:22.850
I call it...

04:23.430 --> 04:25.290
Zombie Tactics!

04:26.640 --> 04:28.290
Wind Slash!

04:39.300 --> 04:41.550
Sunraku

04:41.550 --> 04:42.290
Katzo-kun!

04:42.290 --> 04:43.860
Way ahead of you!

04:43.300 --> 04:45.180
<b>Rebirth Tearjewel</b>

04:45.540 --> 04:47.560
Take that!

05:01.320 --> 05:02.450
Sunraku

05:15.080 --> 05:17.260
I'm tagging in until you're ready!

05:17.260 --> 05:19.360
What'd you learn, Sunraku?!

05:20.200 --> 05:22.180
You can't beat him, so focus on dodging!

05:22.410 --> 05:24.560
Well, simple enough!

05:24.560 --> 05:26.810
You lasted two minutes, five seconds.

05:26.810 --> 05:29.250
That's a record for a first encounter.

05:29.250 --> 05:30.600
Very impressive.

05:31.750 --> 05:34.870
So, what do you think after 
mixing it up with him?

05:34.870 --> 05:38.230
Without one impressive plan, I can tell...

05:38.230 --> 05:41.240
there's definitely no way 
I could keep pace with him.

05:41.910 --> 05:43.490
Wethermon the Tombguard...

05:43.490 --> 05:47.990
He definitely belongs in the 
"Seven Colossi" league with Lycagon.

05:47.990 --> 05:49.500
Wind Slash!

05:51.510 --> 05:55.340
Well, I spent a whole lot of money 
on this "impressive plan"...

05:55.340 --> 05:56.630
So you'd better make it worthwhile.

05:57.110 --> 06:01.300
Four million mahni for a single respawn, huh?

06:03.400 --> 06:04.010
Empire Bee Twinblades
 Marsh Daggers [V3]
 Moonblade (Waxing)

06:03.400 --> 06:04.010
Empire Bee Twinblades
 Category: Twinblade
 Durability
 Attribute: Corrode
 Multiplier: x1.15

06:04.360 --> 06:07.780
Their durability is down to half 
from just two minutes of fighting?!

06:08.160 --> 06:11.020
I guess you really do need a weapon 
with enhanced durability...

06:11.020 --> 06:13.580
Time for the weapon whose durability 
I raised to the extreme...

06:13.580 --> 06:16.060
Marsh Daggers V3!

06:16.600 --> 06:18.610
Resurrection items, weapons...

06:18.610 --> 06:21.760
On all fronts, the battle against 
Wethermon is one of endurance!

06:23.010 --> 06:24.530
I'm tagging in, Katzo!

06:32.790 --> 06:35.170
Okay! I'll take over again if you die!

06:35.170 --> 06:35.790
Right!

06:36.270 --> 06:38.290
Yeah, figured that wouldn't work...

06:42.710 --> 06:43.800
Thunderclap!

06:48.380 --> 06:49.390
Not that easy!

06:50.540 --> 06:52.240
Skate Foot!

06:58.860 --> 07:00.400
Too close!

07:00.740 --> 07:03.900
Thunderclap calls down a five-second 
barrage of insta-kill lightning!

07:03.900 --> 07:05.650
Five damn seconds?!

07:06.780 --> 07:08.860
Okay, I'm getting the hang of this!

07:08.860 --> 07:10.630
Even at close range, if I use Skate Foot

07:10.630 --> 07:13.260
followed by running at max speed, 
I can just keep ahead of it!

07:14.000 --> 07:16.170
Nimbus Fist.

07:24.880 --> 07:27.800
Okay, got no clue on that one.

07:43.320 --> 07:44.520
Tagging in!

07:48.930 --> 07:50.420
Wind Slash!

07:56.500 --> 07:57.660
Tagging in!

07:59.670 --> 08:00.880
Thunderclap!

08:23.380 --> 08:24.650
Screw all this!

08:25.290 --> 08:26.690
I can't dodge that crap!

08:26.690 --> 08:29.650
It'd be a miracle to stay alive for 
even thirty seconds against it!

08:30.080 --> 08:33.420
You've done pretty amazingly, even so.

08:33.420 --> 08:36.160
We still have about half our 
resurrection items left.

08:36.160 --> 08:37.370
You've done very well.

08:37.770 --> 08:40.790
Y'know, you've been playing with 
those scales for a while...

08:41.060 --> 08:42.190
What's it all about?

08:42.190 --> 08:44.290
Just preparing something.

08:44.290 --> 08:46.170
It might be about time to use them, though.

08:55.830 --> 08:57.310
He stopped?

08:58.440 --> 08:59.560
Ten minutes.

09:01.760 --> 09:03.060
Finally there, huh?

09:04.560 --> 09:06.120
Ten minutes have passed.

09:08.320 --> 09:09.800
Phase 2 begins.

09:16.460 --> 09:17.330
E...

09:18.760 --> 09:21.720
Export. Summon Call.

09:22.120 --> 09:23.830
Tactical Mount...

09:23.830 --> 09:25.120
Kirin!

09:32.840 --> 09:34.050
Katzo-kun!

09:34.050 --> 09:35.720
Right, I got this!

09:36.250 --> 09:38.850
Guess my job as resurrection 
backup is over...

09:39.290 --> 09:40.870
Just like the intel said...

09:40.870 --> 09:43.100
When you fight Wethermon for ten minutes,

09:43.100 --> 09:46.940
he summons Kirin, the robot horse!

09:50.940 --> 09:53.940
Okay, so it's a horse...

09:53.940 --> 09:56.580
But it's not exactly what I was picturing.

09:57.020 --> 09:58.270
This is more like...

09:59.060 --> 10:01.960
A dump truck with legs!

10:10.850 --> 10:12.970
Tactical Mount
<b>Kirin</b>

10:22.620 --> 10:24.090
Phase 2.

10:24.090 --> 10:29.610
Wethermon summons Kirin, and you 
must prevent them from combining

10:29.610 --> 10:32.310
while surviving ten minutes, 
just like in Phase 1.

10:32.310 --> 10:34.740
Katzo-kun! You handle Kirin!

10:35.400 --> 10:38.790
If you let him stay in charge, 
he'll fire missiles and lasers everywhere!

10:39.240 --> 10:41.510
And if he combines with Wethermon,

10:41.510 --> 10:43.080
the whole plan'll be done for!

10:43.650 --> 10:45.640
There'll be no way to stop 
them from trampling us,

10:45.640 --> 10:47.760
and it'll be instant death when they do.

10:48.250 --> 10:50.670
The only way to fight that 
is to stay on his back

10:50.670 --> 10:52.960
and trigger his "buck-off animation."

10:52.960 --> 10:55.210
Easier said than done, damn it!

11:04.350 --> 11:06.850
How the hell do you expect me 
to play cowboy with this thing?!

11:06.850 --> 11:11.970
Didn't you play a lot of <i>Cavalry Crisis</i>, 
that mounted fighting game?

11:11.970 --> 11:14.110
Show me your riding technique!

11:14.110 --> 11:16.370
<i>Cavalry Crisis</i>? What the hell is that?!

11:16.370 --> 11:18.620
I've never heard of a 
trash game by that name!

11:18.960 --> 11:21.460
Just focus on your job!

11:21.460 --> 11:22.990
Gotcha!

11:22.990 --> 11:25.410
<i>Cav</i> isn't a trash game!

11:25.410 --> 11:27.220
It's more like a god-tier game!

11:27.220 --> 11:30.660
And that was still just a fighting game...

11:31.000 --> 11:33.000
<i>Okay... how do I do this?</i>

11:38.280 --> 11:41.010
<i></i>SLF<i>'s meticulous with its world-building,</i>

11:41.010 --> 11:43.990
<i>and thinking about that usually 
leads you to a solution...</i>

11:43.990 --> 11:46.520
<i>In other words, if Kirin is a machine,</i>

11:46.520 --> 11:48.410
<i>he'll need maintenance!</i>

11:49.150 --> 11:51.150
There it is! A maintenance ladder!

11:51.370 --> 11:52.650
Expectations met!

11:53.860 --> 11:54.610
Yes!

11:55.990 --> 11:58.590
Every horse needs a bridle, right?!

11:59.060 --> 12:01.810
Skill, "Whip Puppet: Snake"!

12:00.620 --> 12:03.120
<b>Whip Puppet: Snake</b>

12:03.120 --> 12:09.020
Never thought my sub-job, 
"Archaeologist," would pay off like this!

12:10.120 --> 12:14.090
The rodeo technique of the country's 
third-ranked <i>Cavalry Crisis</i> player...

12:14.090 --> 12:17.380
I'll show it to you, you bucking bronco!

12:18.890 --> 12:21.320
Hey!

12:23.010 --> 12:25.140
<u>Use Items</u>
Reward Scales

12:23.440 --> 12:27.400
Sunraku-kun and Katzo-kun are 
holding off their targets,

12:25.140 --> 12:30.770
<u>Offer Items</u>
Silverite Amber

12:27.720 --> 12:31.460
but at this rate, we'll run out of 
resurrection items before we hit the time limit.

12:32.580 --> 12:33.960
Now's the time to use it...

12:34.960 --> 12:36.360
The Reward Scales!

12:38.070 --> 12:49.800
The Golden Scales

12:38.980 --> 12:42.990
<i>The Golden Scales is an 
NPC-run trading company.</i>

12:43.320 --> 12:44.800
<i>In its possession is a</i>

12:44.800 --> 12:49.430
<i>particular "unique item"—a category 
comprising the rarest items in the game.</i>

12:49.800 --> 12:52.630
<i>It is known as the Reward Scales.</i>

12:52.060 --> 12:54.040
<b>Reward Scales</b>

12:53.220 --> 12:56.920
<i>By sacrificing items to the 
left-side "offering dish,"</i>

12:56.920 --> 13:03.740
<i>you can receive various perks from 
the right-side "blessing dish."</i>

13:06.900 --> 13:08.820
Give me the best you've got, Scales.

13:08.820 --> 13:14.360
I did everything I could and finally persuaded 
the Golden Scales to lend you to me.

13:14.780 --> 13:18.280
The Rebirth Tearjewels aren't the only 
thing I dipped into my savings for.

13:18.280 --> 13:23.080
High-value items I've won through my 
exploits, traded for and bought...

13:19.270 --> 13:26.820
<u>Offer Items</u>
Goldblood Ricewine
Crimson Grapewine

13:23.080 --> 13:25.430
Thirty million mahni's worth in total.

13:25.430 --> 13:28.330
And I'm offering it up!

13:30.220 --> 13:33.830
<b>Offering Dish</b>

13:30.220 --> 13:33.830
<b>30,002,310 Mahni</b>

13:33.830 --> 13:35.230
<b>Choose Your Perk</b>

13:35.810 --> 13:37.840
<b>More Stat Points</b>

13:37.840 --> 13:41.620
Nope, nope, nope, nope, nope, 
nope, nope, nope, nope!

13:42.600 --> 13:46.440
The centrifugal force is gonna throw me off!

13:47.400 --> 13:49.850
Damn it! I don't have 
enough stamina for this!

13:49.850 --> 13:51.090
Even if I see the attacks coming,

13:51.090 --> 13:52.940
if my stamina management 
is just a little off,

13:52.940 --> 13:54.940
I fail to dodge it, and I die on the spot!

13:55.600 --> 13:57.690
"The scales maintain equilibrium."

13:58.160 --> 13:59.910
"Let its value be measured numerically."

13:59.910 --> 14:01.440
"Bestow upon me the power to fight hundreds."

14:02.280 --> 14:06.950
Albeit temporarily, I can award 
additional stat points to others...

14:07.520 --> 14:10.300
The rate is one point per 100,000 mahni.

14:10.300 --> 14:12.300
My entire savings—

14:12.300 --> 14:14.210
Three hundred points in total!

14:14.210 --> 14:17.670
Sunraku LV: 50 <b>Mercenary (Twin Blade User)
Oikatzo LV: 50 <b>Monk</b></b>

14:14.830 --> 14:17.670
We'll start off with fifty points each!

14:17.770 --> 14:20.170
<b>Blessings Dish
Perk: Additional Skill Points 300</b>

14:20.170 --> 14:21.920
Take them, you thieves!

14:30.840 --> 14:31.680
Whoa!

14:32.140 --> 14:33.910
<i>My stamina's replenished?</i>

14:33.910 --> 14:36.690
<i>No... my stats have increased!</i>

14:40.440 --> 14:42.610
<i>Pencilgon's behind this, eh?</i>

14:43.240 --> 14:45.940
<i>I was wondering why she was 
fiddling with those windows...</i>

14:46.990 --> 14:49.080
<i>She gave me boosts to stamina and luck!</i>

14:50.070 --> 14:53.630
It's clear I can't deal damage, 
no matter where I hit you...

14:55.430 --> 14:57.290
Weapon unequipped.

14:56.290 --> 14:57.290
<i>But...</i>

14:57.780 --> 14:59.880
Infight!

15:01.210 --> 15:06.430
<i>It's not my first time 
fighting someone like that.</i>

15:08.970 --> 15:14.230
<i>There's a combat skill that doesn't 
pull from strength, but from luck!</i>

15:14.640 --> 15:15.730
<i>Its name...</i>

15:16.750 --> 15:17.850
Wind—

15:17.850 --> 15:21.860
Hand of Fortune!

15:22.150 --> 15:23.250
—Slash!

15:26.210 --> 15:28.490
Hand of Fortune

15:33.010 --> 15:36.750
A swordsman without a sword 
is like curry without roux!

15:37.210 --> 15:39.790
Suck on that! You're just 
a plate of white rice now!

15:39.790 --> 15:42.380
Get yourself some pickled 
plums and try again later!

15:42.380 --> 15:43.340
Skill...

15:45.360 --> 15:47.200
Skate Foot!

15:49.800 --> 15:51.210
Hell yeah!

15:51.210 --> 15:52.900
I got your sword!

15:52.900 --> 15:54.720
How you like that, sucker?!

15:54.720 --> 15:58.730
And it's... so big and heavy!

15:59.290 --> 16:02.260
Can't stick that in inventory, I guess...

16:00.540 --> 16:02.730
Inventory: A player's item storage

16:02.260 --> 16:02.730
But...

16:03.860 --> 16:06.060
Making sure he can't use that 
split-second slash attack

16:06.060 --> 16:08.230
or the lightning strikes is huge!

16:08.230 --> 16:11.070
He's still got that 
Nimbus Fist going on, but...

16:11.680 --> 16:14.540
I'm safe from that as long as I'm behind him.

16:14.540 --> 16:16.960
Knowing that will let 
me avoid it, no problem.

16:17.380 --> 16:18.810
Nice work!

16:20.730 --> 16:23.680
I appreciate you raising my stats and all,

16:23.680 --> 16:26.560
but that's not gonna let me stop this thing!

16:26.560 --> 16:29.470
Katzo-kun! There's about four 
minutes left in Phase 2!

16:29.810 --> 16:32.380
You've got to strap in for that long!

16:32.380 --> 16:34.560
He'll keep to that pattern 
as long as you stay on him!

16:34.820 --> 16:36.810
I get it, but—

16:37.150 --> 16:38.060
<i>Strap</i> in...?

16:45.310 --> 16:47.400
I just got a great idea.

16:47.800 --> 16:49.030
A great idea?

16:51.080 --> 16:53.160
Tidal Rush.

16:57.640 --> 16:59.080
Close call!

16:59.680 --> 17:01.980
I dodged in the nick of time...

17:01.980 --> 17:04.050
But he almost had me there!

17:04.050 --> 17:07.090
That's gotta be an insta-kill, for sure.

17:07.360 --> 17:11.400
They even gave him a special move set 
for if you steal his sword...

17:12.820 --> 17:14.730
This is a bad field layout!

17:14.730 --> 17:15.680
Pencilgon!

17:17.120 --> 17:19.640
I was so focused on evading, 
I ran in the wrong direction!

17:21.680 --> 17:23.220
I turned his aggro on Pencilgon!

17:24.640 --> 17:25.400
Tidal—

17:26.270 --> 17:28.150
Eyes on the prize, Wethermon!

17:29.090 --> 17:31.840
I've still got your sword!

17:35.500 --> 17:38.080
He can grab me from that angle, too?!

17:38.410 --> 17:40.040
Tidal Rush.

17:40.040 --> 17:41.790
Sunraku

17:42.710 --> 17:44.080
Sunraku-kun!

17:48.300 --> 17:50.050
Nimbus Fist.

17:53.460 --> 17:57.070
<i>The safe zone for Nimbus Fist 
is behind Wethermon!</i>

18:02.870 --> 18:05.110
<i>Seven, eight...</i>

18:14.640 --> 18:17.980
Let's get back to basics, Wethermon.

18:19.640 --> 18:21.700
Wind Slash!

18:24.780 --> 18:25.840
Sunraku-kun!

18:25.840 --> 18:29.460
One more death could doom our chances!

18:29.740 --> 18:32.200
If that last attack had been 
anything other than Nimbus Fist,

18:32.200 --> 18:33.470
he could've taken us all out!

18:33.470 --> 18:34.780
Sorry, okay?!

18:34.780 --> 18:39.690
I guess he's better off with the sword! 
At least, I know those animations!

18:39.690 --> 18:41.630
Glad to hear it!

18:42.840 --> 18:43.850
Katzo-kun?!

18:44.120 --> 18:46.350
W-W-Watch this!

18:48.060 --> 18:51.460
H-H-He can't b-b-buck me off like this!

18:51.460 --> 18:54.310
I-I-I can stay on him the whole time!

18:52.850 --> 18:56.280
That... was your great idea?

18:56.280 --> 18:58.860
You want me to go tighter?!

18:58.410 --> 19:02.230
Fine, whatever. If that's what you're into.

19:02.230 --> 19:03.450
What? What's going on?

19:03.450 --> 19:07.630
It's just gonna distract you, 
so it's better if you don't look.

19:07.630 --> 19:08.390
Got it!

19:08.390 --> 19:13.500
Th-The shaking is d-d-raining 
my HP, I th-th-think!

19:13.500 --> 19:17.510
I'm b-b-built to tank damage, b-b-but 
I might not last too long like this!

19:18.800 --> 19:20.080
That's fine.

19:26.730 --> 19:27.600
Huh?

19:53.600 --> 19:56.680
I'm not getting a "you beat me" vibe, here...

19:57.120 --> 19:58.090
Right.

20:08.930 --> 20:11.060
Stay on your guard, both of you.

20:12.570 --> 20:15.930
Even when Ashura Kai was 
a halfway decent clan,

20:15.930 --> 20:19.110
we only made it this far one time.

20:19.640 --> 20:21.010
In other words...

20:21.010 --> 20:23.120
Phase 2 is over.

20:24.650 --> 20:26.560
The real challenge starts now.

20:29.190 --> 20:30.710
Phase 3...

20:37.160 --> 20:40.340
The last time I made it here, he wiped 
out the Ashura Kai with his first move.

20:40.960 --> 20:44.580
When the cracks formed in 
Wethermon the Tombguard's armor...

20:47.170 --> 20:51.310
He let out a howl and unleashed a 
shock wave across the entire field.

20:53.280 --> 20:56.660
When it hit us, all our buffs 
and armor didn't matter a bit.

20:56.660 --> 20:57.920
We died instantly.

20:57.920 --> 21:01.460
Sounds like a pretty solid death sentence...

21:01.460 --> 21:03.740
But you look like you've got a plan.

21:06.830 --> 21:08.770
We'll see about that.

21:07.410 --> 21:09.250
<b>Saint's Holy Water</b>

21:08.770 --> 21:12.250
If this doesn't do the trick, 
try to dodge it as best you can.

21:13.500 --> 21:18.230
In <i>SLF</i>, the keys to victory 
come from the story.

21:18.740 --> 21:22.220
I'd always assumed Wethermon 
was some kind of cyborg,

21:22.220 --> 21:24.830
who'd modified his body with 
technology from the Divinity...

21:25.860 --> 21:26.850
But...

21:26.850 --> 21:33.230
He called Wethermon the Tombguard 
"a living corpse" who'd "outlived his time"?

21:33.440 --> 21:35.910
That's what gave me the key.

21:37.650 --> 21:40.530
His classification is "undead monster"!

21:41.360 --> 21:43.170
For undead, you use holy water!

21:43.810 --> 21:46.520
And that's not just any holy water...

21:46.520 --> 21:49.770
It's holy water the Saint of Love, 
Eristella, put her heart into...

21:49.770 --> 21:51.790
The saint's own holy water!

21:52.230 --> 21:55.320
It's the best potion for fighting 
the undead you can get!

23:42.060 --> 23:49.320
<b>SLF Mini</b>

23:42.840 --> 23:45.850
<i>SLF</i> Theater!

23:45.850 --> 23:49.320
<i><b>The Day Starts Early for a Trash Game Hunter</b></i>

23:46.650 --> 23:48.080
Mini!

23:49.320 --> 26:14.460
<i><b>SLF Theater</b></i>

23:50.820 --> 23:53.330
<i>The day starts early for a trash game hunter.</i>

23:53.720 --> 23:56.220
<b>Why are you up so early?</b>

23:55.240 --> 23:57.760
I'm heading out into the country,

23:57.760 --> 23:59.360
so I needed to catch the first train.

23:59.840 --> 24:01.940
<i>As the trash game hunter 
takes the maglev line west</i>

24:01.940 --> 24:05.100
<i>he watches the scenery out the window.</i>

24:05.100 --> 24:07.570
<i>Mr. Sunraku's gaze is focused.</i>

24:07.570 --> 24:09.040
I got a tip that there's a shop

24:09.040 --> 24:13.990
with an unopened copy of the limited 
edition <i>Moody Music Adventure</i>.

24:13.990 --> 24:16.270
<b>What is <i>Moody Music Adventure</i>?</b>

24:16.270 --> 24:20.880
You know how modern VR games 
are generally soundless?

24:20.880 --> 24:23.840
That is to say, they mostly don't use BGM?

24:23.840 --> 24:25.800
But there are also quite 
a few full-dive VR games

24:25.800 --> 24:28.050
that use BGM as seen in the display copies.

24:28.050 --> 24:30.000
Put simply, most people 
find it annoying and end up

24:30.000 --> 24:31.810
lowering the volume or turning off the BGM,

24:31.810 --> 24:33.970
but this one's a mix between 
rhythm game and action RPG,

24:33.970 --> 24:36.290
and someone had the crazy idea to not 
let you turn the BGM volume down.

24:36.290 --> 24:37.710
So it's this trash game where you

24:37.710 --> 24:39.280
have to do rhythm game stuff 
with this really annoying BGM.

24:39.280 --> 24:41.760
The limited edition comes packaged 
with the main character's headphones.

24:41.760 --> 24:44.460
That nice and all, but who'd 
want to wear the headphones you

24:44.460 --> 24:47.120
associate with this BGM 
that gives you a headache?

24:47.120 --> 24:51.840
<i>As he speaks on with the 
force of a raging bonfire,</i>

24:51.840 --> 24:57.890
<i>there is a bitterness in his tone, 
combined with a strange sense of delight.</i>

24:58.800 --> 25:02.360
<i>After getting a brief 
breakfast at the station,</i>

25:02.360 --> 25:04.530
<i>he arrives at the shop in question.</i>

25:04.530 --> 25:07.650
<i>But his eyes are harsh.</i>

25:08.040 --> 25:10.540
<b>What are you doing?</b>

25:09.230 --> 25:10.540
Look at this.

25:11.000 --> 25:12.510
It's a folding chair.

25:13.130 --> 25:14.690
It's still warm.

25:14.690 --> 25:16.180
Have they been here since 
before the first train?

25:17.130 --> 25:20.400
This is the sign of a 
crazy trash game hunter.

25:20.760 --> 25:24.550
<i>With his hand to the lingering 
warmth upon the folding chair,</i>

25:24.550 --> 25:28.080
<i>Mr. Sunraku scours the area around him.</i>

25:28.390 --> 25:31.790
There's no way there are two limited 
edition unopened copies in there.

25:32.370 --> 25:33.510
Which means...

25:33.870 --> 25:37.930
The moment the shop opens, 
we'll have to both run for it.

25:38.370 --> 25:42.280
<i>Trash game—it refers to the 
content of the game itself.</i>

25:42.280 --> 25:47.940
<i>Mr. Sunraku undergoes a focused warm-up 
routine as his eyes gaze ahead.</i>

25:48.560 --> 25:50.970
<i>At times, he must even fight his own kind...</i>

25:50.970 --> 25:54.370
<i>But there's a smile on his lips.</i>

25:55.700 --> 25:57.310
So, how'd it go?

25:57.760 --> 25:59.030
You get into a brawl?

25:59.030 --> 26:00.020
Nah.

26:00.020 --> 26:02.880
The person was there for 
something totally different.

26:02.880 --> 26:06.200
So it wasn't a crazy trash game hunter, huh?

26:07.530 --> 26:10.490
What do you mean, "crazy trash game hunter"?

26:12.160 --> 26:13.960
Please don't ask me that.
